{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2178-07-13 16:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello, Mr. ___. I'm Dr. ___, one of your hospital doctors. I see you're here because of poor nutrition and to get a feeding tube and a new line for your treprostinil."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2178-07-13 16:12:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, that’s right. I’ve been losing weight and just can’t eat much. Food tastes bad since I started the treprostinil."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2178-07-13 16:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. That’s a known side effect. We’re going to help you with a Dobhoff tube so you can get nutrition even if you’re not eating well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2178-07-13 16:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my tunneled line? I’ve been using the PICC, but it’s not ideal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2178-07-13 16:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll replace the tunneled line tomorrow. It’s safer for long-term treprostinil use. The PICC is temporary."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2178-07-13 16:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I manage the pump myself, so I want it to be reliable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2178-07-13 16:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You do a great job managing it. We’ll make sure the new line is secure and ready for home use."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2178-07-13 16:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your labs show low white blood cells and platelets, which is expected with cirrhosis. We’ll monitor that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2178-07-13 16:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had low platelets for a while. Is it safe to do the procedures?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2178-07-13 16:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll use normal platelets if needed. The team is aware, and we’ll take precautions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2178-07-13 16:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We also noticed your kidney function has improved. Creatinine is now 1.2, much better than before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2178-07-13 16:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. I was worried after last time with the kidney issues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2178-07-13 16:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, last admission was tough with the infection and pneumonia. But you cleared the bacteremia, and now we’re focusing on getting you stronger for transplant."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2178-07-13 16:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I really want to be ready. That’s why I want the feeding tube."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2178-07-13 16:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. Nutrition is key. The team recommends Isosource at 65 cc/hr once the tube is placed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2178-07-14 12:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. We just finished the paracentesis and tunneled line placement. Five liters of fluid were removed, and the new line is in place."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2178-07-14 12:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "How did it go? I was asleep, but I feel okay now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2178-07-14 12:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It went very well. The line is single-lumen, volume 1.1 mL, and it’s already connected. Treprostinil is running through it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2178-07-14 12:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. And the fluid removal? My belly felt so full."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2178-07-14 12:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, the ascites was significant. The fluid looked clean, and the white count was low—no sign of infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2178-07-14 12:40:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So no spontaneous bacterial peritonitis this time?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2178-07-14 12:42:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, the culture came back negative. You’re on ciprofloxacin for prevention, which is helping."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2178-07-14 12:44:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll keep monitoring your oxygen too. You’re still on nighttime O2 for hepatopulmonary syndrome."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2178-07-14 12:46:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I use it every night. My pulse ox was 93 on room air yesterday."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2178-07-14 12:48:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s why we keep the O2. It helps with the low oxygen levels from liver disease."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2178-07-15 13:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi again. We placed the Dobhoff tube yesterday during endoscopy. The X-ray confirms it’s past the pylorus, in good position."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2178-07-15 13:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I didn’t feel a thing. Is it safe to start the feeds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2178-07-15 13:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ve started Isosource at 65 cc/hr. We’ll keep an eye on your stomach for any bloating or discomfort."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2178-07-15 13:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And I’ll keep taking megace? It’s helped my appetite a little."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2178-07-15 13:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, you’ll continue megace, mirtazapine, and fluoxetine. They help with appetite and mood."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2178-07-15 13:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your liver numbers are stable. MELD is around 13, which is good for now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2178-07-15 13:12:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Lower than last time?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2178-07-15 13:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, last admission it was 17. Your kidney function improved, which helps lower the score."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2178-07-15 13:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So that’s good for transplant listing?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2178-07-15 13:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It means your body is more stable. We want you strong and well-nourished when a liver becomes available."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2178-07-16 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your labs today look better. Creatinine is down to 0.9, and bicarbonate is normalizing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2178-07-16 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. Any change in the feeding?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2178-07-16 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, we’re keeping the feeds at goal. You’re tolerating them well—no vomiting or diarrhea."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2178-07-16 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your platelets are up to 30, still low but stable. No need for transfusion."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2178-07-16 10:08:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my back pain? It’s been okay with the morphine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2178-07-16 10:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll keep your MS Contin and dilaudid for breakthrough. Osteoporosis and old fractures make it chronic, but we can manage it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2178-07-16 10:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We also checked your calcium and vitamin D. You’re on supplements, which is important."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2178-07-16 10:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I take them every day. Don’t want more fractures."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2178-07-17 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news—discharge today. You’re doing well. The feeding tube and new line are working, and you’ve had no complications."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2178-07-17 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. What do I need to do at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2178-07-17 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Continue all your meds, including ciprofloxacin, lactulose, and rifaximin. The feeding will continue at 65 cc/hr."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2178-07-17 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The supply company will deliver your tube feeds and pump supplies today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2178-07-17 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the tunneled line care?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2178-07-17 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Keep the dressing clean and dry. Change it weekly or if wet. Call if redness, swelling, or fever."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2178-07-17 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Weigh yourself daily. Call if you gain more than 3 pounds in a day—could be fluid building up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2178-07-17 08:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And follow-up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2178-07-17 08:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, labs in a few days—chem 10, CBC, coags, liver tests. Fax them to your hepatology team."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2178-07-17 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll make sure my sister helps me with that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2178-07-17 08:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "She’s listed as your contact—good to have support. Keep all your transplant clinic appointments."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2178-07-17 08:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m hopeful. I feel better already with the feeds starting."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2178-07-17 08:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s the goal. Nutrition, stability, and readiness. You’re on the right track."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2178-07-17 08:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor. I appreciate everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2178-07-17 08:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. We’ll see you in follow-up. Take care, and call if anything changes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2178-07-17 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Have a good day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2178-07-17 08:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You too. The discharge nurse will go over everything one more time before you leave."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2178-07-17 08:34:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, sounds good."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2178-07-17 08:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One last thing—keep using sildenafil and the oxygen at night. They help your lung pressures."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2178-07-17 08:38:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I haven’t missed a dose."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2178-07-17 08:40:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. That’s all for now. Rest up and keep building your strength."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2178-07-17 08:42:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2178-07-17 08:44:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing great. See you soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2178-07-17 08:46:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Bye, Doctor."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2178-07-13 16:04:00",
    "admission_end": "2178-07-17 12:40:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "Mr. ___ was admitted for placement of a Dobhoff feeding tube and replacement of his tunneled central line due to malnutrition and ongoing treprostinil therapy for portopulmonary hypertension. He reported significant anorexia and weight loss attributed to treprostinil, despite using megestrol to improve appetite. A tunneled line was successfully placed on hospital day two, and a Dobhoff tube was inserted endoscopically the following day, with radiographic confirmation of correct placement. Tube feeds were initiated and tolerated well. Five liters of ascitic fluid were removed during paracentesis, with no signs of infection. His kidney function improved, with creatinine normalizing, and liver enzymes remained stable. He was discharged home with services to continue tube feeds, treprostinil via the new line, and all home medications, including ciprofloxacin for SBP prophylaxis. Outpatient follow-up and lab monitoring were arranged.",
    "problems": [
      "Unspecified protein-calorie malnutrition",
      "Cirrhosis of liver without mention of alcohol",
      "Hepatopulmonary syndrome",
      "Awaiting organ transplant status",
      "Thrombocytopenia, unspecified",
      "Other chronic pain",
      "Depressive disorder, not elsewhere classified"
    ]
  }
}
